## Anti-Patterns to Avoid
- ❌ Do NOT deep-merge the two `mulligan` objects (spec/09 §1 mandates top-level replace; validateConfig fills sub-key defaults).
- ❌ Do NOT read the local file when isTrusted !== true (fail-safe; privacy for untrusted projects).
- ❌ Do NOT import `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` or any local module — it breaks unit-testability and violates the pure-tier invariant.
- ❌ Do NOT cache the result inside the loader (the caller owns cache via config.ts:setConfig).
- ❌ Do NOT validate/coerce the mulligan value here — config.ts:validateConfig owns that. Returning non-object mulligan AS-IS is correct.
- ❌ Do NOT wire the loader into src/index.ts in this task (that is P1.M1.T2.S1 — scope boundary).
- ❌ Do NOT let console.warn throw (wrap it in try/catch like config.ts:warnConfig).
- ❌ Do NOT use truthiness to detect the mulligan key (`{mulligan:null}` IS present → null wins; use hasOwnProperty).
